    "raw_reply": "The Ohio Attorney General\u2019s Office is a government agency, not a private corporation, so titles like CEO, Founder, Country Head, and AI Head do not exist within its structure. The agency is led by Attorney General Andy Wilson, who serves as the state's chief legal officer and was appointed by Governor Mike DeWine; his email is Andy.Wilson@OhioAttorneyGeneral.gov. Chief of Staff Benjamin Marrison oversees all non-legal operations, including IT and finance, at Benjamin.Marrison@OhioAttorneyGeneral.gov. Chief Information Officer Mark Edwards leads the Information Technology Services department, with email Mark.Edwards@OhioAttorneyGeneral.gov. Chief Data and Analytics Officer Shravan Kotha oversees business intelligence, analytics, and data management, serving in a role equivalent to an AI head, at Shravan.Kotha@OhioAttorneyGeneral.gov. The office has no single human founder; it was created as a statutory office by the Ohio General Assembly in 1846 and became an elected position in 1851.",
