    "raw_reply": "A Head of Technology is often the same as a Chief Technology Officer (CTO) in smaller organizations\n, but they are typically distinct roles in larger companies.\nSplunk\nRole Differences\nCTO (Chief Technology Officer):\nAn executive-level C-suite role focused on long-term strategy, company vision, external products, and aligning tech with overall business goals.\nZipRecruiter\nHead of Technology:\nA senior management role that usually focuses more on day-to-day operations, team management, and project execution.\nZipRecruiter\nHierarchy and Overlap\nIn startups or mid-sized businesses, the titles are frequently used interchangeably to mean the top technology leader.\nIn larger enterprises, a Head of Technology may report directly to the CTO or a Chief Information Officer (CIO), managing specific departments or regional tech teams.\nSplunk\nThe Chief Technology Officer Role: Skills, Responsibilities, and Career ...\nCTO vs. CIO vs CPO: What's the difference? The CIO (Chief Information Officer) handles internal IT infrastructure and operations a...\nZipRecruiter\nWhat is the difference between Head Of Technology vs CTO? - ZipRecruiter\nThe Head Of Technology typically manages day-to-day tech operations and teams, focusing on project execution. The CTO holds a stra...\nSplunk\nThe Chief Technology Officer Role: Skills, Responsibilities, and Career ...\nCTO vs. CIO vs CPO: What's the difference? The CIO (Chief Information Officer) handles internal IT infrastructure and operations a...\nZipRecruiter\nWhat is the difference between Head Of Technology vs CTO? - ZipRecruiter\nThe Head Of Technology typically manages day-to-day tech operations and teams, focusing on project execution. The CTO holds a stra...\nShow less",
